;docs/ai_digest/alien_nodes.md: what goes over a TCP link, the two kinds of packet
(defq s (dia-scene) blue 0xffd7e6f7 green 0xffdff0d8 gold 0xffffe8a8 grey 0xfff2f4f6 red 0xfff7d7d7 dark 0xff202428)
(dia-say s "a ping, each second each way, 48 bytes" 0 14 12 :t dark)
(dia-put s 'p0 (dia-box '("length 40" "uint") 80 44 blue 11) 0 30)
(dia-put s 'p1 (dia-box '("type 1" "uint") 80 44 blue 11) 80 30)
(dia-put s 'p2 (dia-box '("node id" "16 bytes") 100 44 green 11) 160 30)
(dia-put s 'p3 (dia-box '("system id" "16 bytes") 100 44 green 11) 260 30)
(dia-put s 'p4 (dia-box '("task count" "uint, its load") 110 44 green 11) 360 30)
(dia-put s 'p5 (dia-box '("to 8" "pad") 60 44 grey 11) 470 30)
(dia-say s "a fragment of a message, 72 bytes and its data" 0 104 12 :t dark)
(dia-put s 'f0 (dia-box '("length" "uint") 70 44 blue 11) 0 120)
(dia-put s 'f1 (dia-box '("type 2" "uint") 70 44 blue 11) 70 120)
(dia-put s 'f2 (dia-box '("dest" "24 bytes, net id") 110 44 gold 11) 140 120)
(dia-put s 'f3 (dia-box '("src" "24 bytes, net id") 110 44 gold 11) 250 120)
(dia-put s 'f4 (dia-box '("length, offset," "total, uints") 120 44 gold 11) 360 120)
(dia-put s 'f5 (dia-box '("data, up to" "6104 bytes") 120 44 red 11) 480 120)
(dia-say s "The first two uints are the wire header, the length of what follows it and its type. A net id is a mailbox id, 8 bytes," 0 190 11)
(dia-say s "and a node id, 16. A message bigger than one fragment goes as several, its offset and total say where each goes." 0 206 11)
(dia-say s "On a sealed link each packet goes inside a record, mesh_net.md." 0 222 11)
(diagram "link_packet" (dia-scene-doc s))
